{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head c02593659b215178f068efd257dee0ed4b5bccce on planner/artroom-scope-enforce-20261111, all four artifacts, for S2, request fa21cfa5, under promise 1d5998df and review request f48f456e. The tracked file of artroom-scope selects `enforce`, and its comment, the configuration test and the two security pages say the same.\n\nWhat I checked at the head:\n\n- The mode. In `packages/scope/src/scope-index.ts:144-146`, a scope that the index does not list returns `missing` before the Worker gets a target object, unless the mode is `register`. Only the exact string `register` selects register mode (`scope-index.ts:71-72`). So `trust-boundaries.md` is right that a read of an unknown ID reaches no target object.\n- The old objects. `registerKnown` (`packages/scope/src/object.ts:524`) refuses an object without a verified applied genesis whose seed names the scope, so an empty object that an unknown ID made in register mode never got an index row. The statement \"The index lists none of them\" holds.\n- The inventory. The primary artifact records steps 1 and 2: the operator room's 9 scopes, listed and swept in register mode with 9 verified and 0 mismatches (`07-sweep-register-mode.json` under `~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-11-artroom-scope-enforce`). It names the rooms under the Start register that no key reaches, and request fa21cfa5 accepts that those rooms answer a refusal after the deployment.\n- Stale text. No other page says that artroom-scope runs `register`. `docs/security/settings.md` describes both modes in general terms and stays true. The October notes that show `--var SCOPE_INDEX_MODE:register` are dated records of that rollout.\n- The comment. It says to deploy with no `--var` override of the setting, as ruling 5b38cde5 requires.\n\nChecks:\n\n- Scope. Main 74c958d0 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the planner's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the four paths that its four artifacts cover. The commit-message check passes with 1 checked and 0 flagged, `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean.\n- On my own extracted copy of the head: `packages/cli/test/demo-config.test.ts` passes 4 of 4, `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs` and `scripts/security-settings.test.mjs` pass 15 of 15, and `check-doc-links.mjs` checks 1,234 local links and finds none broken.\n\nArchitecture: sound. All eight Worker files under `apps/room/` now select one mode, and the setting lives in the reviewed file instead of a deploy-time override.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The head closes finding 1.5 of review 79daff0f once the deployment runs: an unknown, well-formed scope ID no longer makes a new object with the full schema. The cost is the one that request fa21cfa5 accepts: a room under the Start register that no request reached since 23 October answers a refusal. Its data stays, and a deploy of version fa9d6f64 restores it.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One note: the threat model says the index \"lists each scope that a request reached\" in register mode. Strictly, it lists each reached scope whose object holds a verified genesis. An unknown ID that a request reached made no row. The trust-boundaries paragraph says so, so the two pages together are exact.\n\nThis approval authorizes no deployment. The planner runs step 4 with its START and END acts, and checks that a listed scope answers and that an unknown ID answers the enforce refusal.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fe436982b96bc5cf3d974207d0ce84d3ac5850f0","binding":"assigned","head":"c02593659b215178f068efd257dee0ed4b5bccce","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2d0ca1657f3ba56a8e746a178c7129f0166ec9a7\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1d5998df249d0e3e8dc3922c9e1265020959d754\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f757